Subject: [PATCH] [proxying] Signal before unlock in emscripten_proxy_finish/cancel_ctx

Backport of emscripten-core/emscripten#26582 to 3.1.56.

A SYNC em_proxying_ctx lives on the CALLER's stack (emscripten_proxy_sync_with_ctx).
emscripten_proxy_finish and cancel_ctx set the state, UNLOCK the mutex, and only then
pthread_cond_signal the ctx's cond. A caller that was not yet waiting can take the mutex in
that window, see DONE/CANCELED, return and reuse its stack; the signal then runs on garbage.
musl's cond lock() spins forever on any _c_lock value other than 0 or 2, which is the observed
100%-CPU hang in __private_cond_signal <- emscripten_proxy_finish <- call_with_ctx <-
em_task_queue_execute <- emscripten_proxy_execute_queue, on the wasmfs OPFS ProxyWorker's
heartbeat (ikvmcraft world load, dotnet-runtime-jspi MINECRAFT-FINDINGS R316 addendum 4).
Signalling while still holding the mutex closes the window: the caller cannot observe the new
state until the unlock.

--- a/system/lib/pthread/proxying.c	2026-09-26 14:05:02.140146730 -0700
+++ b/system/lib/pthread/proxying.c	2026-09-26 14:05:02.178141027 -0700
@@ -323,8 +323,11 @@
     pthread_mutex_lock(&ctx->sync.mutex);
     ctx->sync.state = DONE;
     remove_active_ctx(ctx);
-    pthread_mutex_unlock(&ctx->sync.mutex);
+    // Signal must come before unlock to avoid emscripten_proxy_sync_with_ctx
+    // seeing the state as DONE and freeing the ctx before we call signal.
+    // Backport of https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/pull/26582
     pthread_cond_signal(&ctx->sync.cond);
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&ctx->sync.mutex);
   } else {
     // Schedule the callback on the caller thread. If the caller thread has
     // already died or dies before the callback is executed, then at least make
@@ -349,8 +352,9 @@
   if (ctx->kind == SYNC) {
     pthread_mutex_lock(&ctx->sync.mutex);
     ctx->sync.state = CANCELED;
-    pthread_mutex_unlock(&ctx->sync.mutex);
+    // Signal must be first, see comment in emscripten_proxy_finish.
     pthread_cond_signal(&ctx->sync.cond);
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&ctx->sync.mutex);
   } else {
     if (ctx->cb.cancel == NULL ||
         !do_proxy(ctx->cb.queue,
